    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nI think it would be helpful to support arrays in the initialization of the triggers,\n\nwould change something like\n``` lua\n\n          { mode = 'n',          keys = \"'\" },\n          { mode = 'n',          keys = '`' },\n          { mode = 'x',          keys = \"'\" },\n          { mode = 'x',          keys = '`' },\n\n```\nto this\n``` lua\n          { mode = { 'n', 'x' }, keys = { \"'\", '`' } },\n\n```",
